        to origin/main before the three fixes below were applied.

SUMMARY: 52 passed, 0 failed.

This run is the AFTER arm of three fixes. The BEFORE arm (same drill, same
rig, pre-fix) is recorded in the notes below, because two of its legs are
what the fixes were written against.

  D0  a race for a fresh cell resolves to exactly one writer; the loser parks
      in claimingEpoch at 0/6 quiet polls while the holder's token moves.
  D1  a push at the standby is refused, and the refusal NAMES the posture and
      the prefix. Before: 'the repository server is not accepting writes (No
      such file or directory (os error 2))' — the socket did not exist yet.
      After:  'another server holds c8/one; this process is a standby and
               cannot publish — push to the repository's own endpoint, or
               wait for it to take over'
  D2  6 rounds of simultaneous pushes at both doors: holder acked 6/6, standby
      acked 0/6, and the challenger cost the holder nothing.
  D3  CONTROL: the same generator with the two servers on DIFFERENT prefixes.
      Both ack. The rig CAN observe two writers succeeding, so D2's asymmetry
      is the lease and not the harness.
  D4  the holder is SIGSTOPped: the standby supersedes after the quiet window
      and the epoch advances (2 -> 3).
  D5  SIGCONT: the deposed server names its deposal and EXITS rather than
      serve on — the fence is the loop's exit. A push into it is refused and
      the cell still names the successor.
  D6  ORACLE: both servers stopped, a third restores into an EMPTY repository
      from S3 alone. 8 acked refs present, 8 refused refs absent, exactly.
  D7  a standby with PREWARM=0 and no repository yet CREATES and CONFIGURES
      one before it claims, and refuses by posture. Before the fix this leg
      met 'cannot find hook proc-receive' — safe, but naming nothing.
  D7a a bare repository forge did not create, beside a parked syncer. Before
      the fix plain git ACCEPTED the push and the client was told its commit
      had landed when nothing reached the bucket. Now forge takes the
      repository over at startup and the push is refused.

